{ Regression test: two units in different directories share the unit name
  `util`. They must be treated as distinct modules (identity by file path),
  not deduplicated by unit name. If the loader collapses them, whoB (defined
  only in b/util) would be missing and this test would fail to compile. }
program ModuleNameCollision;
uses a/util, b/util;

begin
  writeln('a=', who());
  writeln('b=', whoB());
end.
